English Short Note & Answers
Objects: Containers holding data in key-value pairs (e.g., { name: 'Ben' }).
Classes: Blueprints used to create multiple objects with the same structure and behaviors.
Prototypes: A template object that other objects link to. Every JS object has a prototype chain.
Class vs. Prototype: Classes act as strict blueprints to build objects from scratch. Prototypes act as
an existing base object that you can directly copy and modify dynamically.
Inheritance: The mechanism where one object acquires properties and methods from another (a
parent). This can be achieved via extends (Classes) or Object.create() (Prototypes).
