JavaScript Basics and Prototypes

Prototype Pollution: A vulnerability in JavaScript where an attacker modifies the base prototype of an
object. Because objects inherit properties from their prototypes, this malicious modification is
propagated to all existing and newly created objects in the application.
The __proto__ property: A special property in JavaScript that points to an object's prototype.
Attackers often use __proto__ to traverse up the prototype chain and inject malicious code or
properties (e.g., object.__proto__.malicious = "hacked").
Impact: Even if a single object is compromised via __proto__, it pollutes the blueprint, causing all
other instances (like josh in the example) to inherit the modified, polluted behavior.
